 "notes": {
  "circle": "Developer-controlled wallets bill per monthly active wallet, one that \"conducted an on-chain transaction\" that month, with no fee per transaction. All-included plan (signing, indexing, broadcasting), graduated by band. A bot's 20 wallets sit inside the free 1,000 at any volume.",
  "coinbase-cdp": "\"Pricing is consistent across wallet types\": server wallets on API-key authentication bill the same operations as embedded ones. Sending a transaction (sign and broadcast) is 2 operations. A policy evaluation is 1 more; these scenarios configure no policy. Creating an account is 1 operation, once.",
  "crossmint": "Free up to 1,000 wallets and 2,000 transactions. Beyond, two different rates ($0.025 and \"starts at $0.02\") and no self-serve paid plan, so a larger workload is a quote.",
  "dfns": "Self-service annual or quarterly plans; monthly figures are the annual price over twelve. Each plan includes a number of wallets and of signatures a month, with no published overage: beyond, \"Talk to us\". \"No transaction fees.\"",
  "lit": "Prepaid credits, no subscription. A Lit Action is billed $0.01 per second and \"standard ECDSA signatures are effectively charged at $0.01\"; priced at $0.01 a transaction, sign only (broadcasting is the customer's, and an action that also broadcasts runs longer). Paying in LITKEY is 25% less; the card price is used.",
  "magic": "Server wallets on Express or Core \"count when they successfully sign\". Every successful signing request counts against 50,000 a month per team. Magic signs; broadcasting is the customer's.",
  "openfort": "Backend wallets are in every plan. A payment is \"two operations: sign, then broadcast\". A project without a paid subscription \"stops at the included limit\" with HTTP 402, while the Free card offers $0.01 per operation once a payment method is added; the Free plan is priced as stopping at 2,000.",
  "portal": "Start-Up includes 1K monthly operations and 1K wallets, each $0.10 beyond. Operations are \"Generate, Backup, Sign, Recover, Eject\"; a transaction is one Sign. Whether the wallet overage is charged once or every month is not stated (priced every month, the higher reading), and the Developer plan is a development environment only.",
  "privy": "Server wallets have no Privy user, so only signatures are billed: 50,000 a month free, then pay-as-you-go at a $2,000 base and $0.01 per signature. Privy also bills apps above $1M of monthly transaction volume \"based on usage\" at a rate it does not publish; a real payout or trading flow is likely to cross it, so every Privy price here is a lower bound.",
  "thirdweb": "Server wallets bill per API request: 1,000 included, then $1, $0.60 and $0.20 per thousand at 100K and 250K. A transaction is one request that signs and sends. Priced band by band; whether the lower rate applies to the whole count is not stated.",
  "turnkey": "Billed per signature; Turnkey's own broadcasting is priced on request and not included. Pay as You Go holds up to 1,000 wallets and Pro 2,000; beyond, Enterprise has no published price."
 },
